The synonym "branchial muscle" is related but not identical to "chordate pharyngeal muscle." The term "branchial" specifically refers to structures related to the gills or pharyngeal arches, which are part of the pharynx but not exclusively muscles. "Chordate pharyngeal muscle" is more specific to the muscles acting on the pharynx in chordates, which includes a broader range of muscles beyond just those associated with the gills or pharyngeal arches. Therefore, while they are related, they are not exact synonyms.
